From 3a03407bc93ab091e64d374d629605aa8ed14160 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:03:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/55] Switch: TPIDR_EL0 bridge and emulator VA-reservation
 compatibility.

nx_tls_bridge.c copies the libnx soft thread pointer into TPIDR_EL0 on every
thread (wrapped threadCreate) so the Rust code (NAK) inside the Mesa 26.2.4
Horizon SDK finds its thread-local storage.

nx_nvcompat.c detects emulators whose fixed NVGPU_AS_IOCTL_ALLOC_SPACE answers
with the start of the free block and then reserves the big-page region once;
it does nothing on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
